   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Venetian Blinds\n\nThe outgoing scene is cut into horizontal slats that turn edge-on one after another, like blinds opening onto the next scene. Built-in placeholder scenes A and B (the two .vnb-panel elements) make it preview on its own; to use it between your own scenes, replace the contents of those two panels with your scenes (or set them to your full-frame clips) and keep the block on a track above.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 0.8667 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A crisp, architectural scene change with a visible rhythm.\n- Office, real-estate, corporate or editorial pieces that want a tidy reveal.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The scenes are very busy: the slat edges add visual noise.\n- You want a soft, organic change.\n\nVariables:\n- slats (number, 2-40): Slats, default 12\n- stagger (number, 0-0.9): Stagger, default 0.55\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"top-down\"\n- shade_color (color): Shade color, default \"#000000\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Venetian Blinds\n\n  The outgoing scene is cut into horizontal slats that turn edge-on one after another, like blinds opening onto the next scene.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/venetian-blinds/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"venetian-blinds\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"0.8667\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"slats\",\n    \"type\": \"number\",\n    \"role\": \"layout\",\n    \"label\": \"Slats\",\n    \"description\": \"Number of horizontal slats.\",\n    \"default\": 12,\n    \"min\": 2,\n    \"max\": 40,\n    \"step\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"stagger\",\n    \"type\": \"number\",\n    \"role\": \"motion\",\n    \"label\": \"Stagger\",\n    \"description\": \"Share of the transition spent rippling across slats, 0 to 0.9.\",\n    \"default\": 0.55,\n    \"min\": 0,\n    \"max\": 0.9,\n    \"step\": 0.05\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"direction\",\n    \"type\": \"enum\",\n    \"role\": \"motion\",\n    \"label\": \"Direction\",\n    \"description\": \"Which slat turns first.\",\n    \"default\": \"top-down\",\n    \"options\": [\n      {\n        \"value\": \"top-down\",\n        \"label\": \"Top down\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"value\": \"bottom-up\",\n        \"label\": \"Bottom up\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"value\": \"center\",\n        \"label\": \"From the center\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"shade_color\",\n    \"type\": \"color\",\n    \"role\": \"style\",\n    \"label\": \"Shade color\",\n    \"description\": \"Tint a slat picks up as it turns away from the light.\",\n    \"default\": \"#000000\"\n  }\n]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Venetian Blinds</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: #141318; }\n        .vnb-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .vnb-panel { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden; }\n        .vnb-in { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 2.4cqmin; }\n        .vnb-in span { font-size: 9cqmin; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1; color: #f2f2f2; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .vnb-bar { display: block; width: 14cqmin; height: 0.8cqmin; border-radius: 1cqmin; background: rgba(242, 242, 242, 0.55); }\n        .vnb-pa { background: #141318; }\n        .vnb-pb { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b3699 0%, #1e2a6b 55%, #0f4c75 100%); }\n        .vnb-pc { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7a2f5f 0%, #3a2250 55%, #1c1b3f 100%); }\n\n        .vnb-slats { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 2; }\n        .vnb-slat { position: absolute; left: 0; overflow: hidden; transform-origin: 50% 50%; backface-visibility: hidden; }\n        .vnb-slat > .vnb-copy { position: absolute; left: 0; }\n        .vnb-shade { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .vnb-pb { z-index: 1; }\n        #vnb-pa-src { display: none; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"venetian-blinds\" data-duration=\"0.8667\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"vnb-clip\" class=\"vnb-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"0.8667\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"vnb-src\" style=\"display:none\"><div id=\"vnb-a\" class=\"vnb-panel vnb-pa\"><div class=\"vnb-in\"><span>Scene A</span><i class=\"vnb-bar\"></i></div></div></div>\n          <div id=\"vnb-b\" class=\"vnb-panel vnb-pb\"><div class=\"vnb-in\"><span>Scene B</span><i class=\"vnb-bar\"></i></div></div>\n          <div id=\"vnb-slats\" class=\"vnb-slats\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        \n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\nvar root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\nvar vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\nfunction num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\nfunction str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v.trim() : f; }\nfunction pick(v, list, f) { return list.indexOf(String(v)) >= 0 ? String(v) : f; }\nfunction clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : x > 1 ? 1 : x; }\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\nfunction smooth(a, b, x) { var t = clamp01((x - a) / (b - a)); return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); }\n// cubic-bezier easing, solved by bisection (pure function of x)\nfunction bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n  return function (x) {\n    if (x <= 0) return 0;\n    if (x >= 1) return 1;\n    var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n    for (var i = 0; i < 28; i++) {\n      var cx = 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * x1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n      if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n      t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n    }\n    return 3 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) * t * y1 + 3 * (1 - t) * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n  };\n}\nvar inOutEase = bez(0.42, 0, 0.58, 1);\nfunction inCubic(x) { return x * x * x; }\nfunction outCubic(x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); }\nfunction inQuad(x) { return x * x; }\nfunction outQuad(x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); }\nfunction outBack(s) { return function (x) { return 1 + (s + 1) * Math.pow(x - 1, 3) + s * Math.pow(x - 1, 2); }; }\n// interpolate(p, inputs, outputs, ease): clamped, eased per segment (like a frame interpolate)\nfunction interp(p, xs, ys, ease) {\n  var n = xs.length;\n  if (p <= xs[0]) return ys[0];\n  if (p >= xs[n - 1]) return ys[n - 1];\n  for (var i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n    if (p <= xs[i]) {\n      var t = (p - xs[i - 1]) / (xs[i] - xs[i - 1]);\n      if (ease) t = ease(t);\n      return lerp(ys[i - 1], ys[i], t);\n    }\n  }\n  return ys[n - 1];\n}\nfunction mulberry32(a) {\n  return function () {\n    a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n    var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n    t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  };\n}\n// damped spring from 0 to 1 (zero initial velocity), t in seconds\nfunction spring(t, damping, stiffness, mass) {\n  if (t <= 0) return 0;\n  var w0 = Math.sqrt(stiffness / mass), z = damping / (2 * Math.sqrt(stiffness * mass));\n  if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-4) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n  if (z < 1) {\n    var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n    return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n  }\n  var s = Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -w0 * (z - s), r2 = -w0 * (z + s);\n  return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n}\nfunction stripIds(node) {\n  var all = node.querySelectorAll(\"[id]\");\n  for (var i = 0; i < all.length; i++) all[i].removeAttribute(\"id\");\n  node.removeAttribute(\"id\");\n  return node;\n}\nfunction drive(name, duration, frame) {\n  var st = { p: 0 };\n  frame(0);\n  var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n  tl.to(st, { p: 1, duration: duration, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { frame(st.p); } }, 0);\n  tl.seek(0);\n  window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n  window.__timelines[name] = tl;\n}\n\n            var D = 0.8667;\n\nvar count = Math.round(num(vars.slats, 12, 2, 40)), spread = num(vars.stagger, 0.55, 0, 0.9);\nvar dir = pick(vars.direction, [\"top-down\", \"bottom-up\", \"center\"], \"top-down\");\nvar shade = str(vars.shade_color, \"#000000\");\nvar host = document.getElementById(\"vnb-slats\"), src = document.getElementById(\"vnb-a\"), B = document.getElementById(\"vnb-b\");\nvar W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\nhost.style.perspective = H * 2.2 + \"px\";\nhost.style.perspectiveOrigin = \"50% 50%\";\nvar turn = bez(0.55, 0, 0.35, 1);\nvar slats = [];\nfor (var i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n  var top = Math.floor(i * H / count), bottom = Math.floor((i + 1) * H / count);\n  var el = document.createElement(\"div\");\n  el.className = \"vnb-slat\";\n  el.style.top = top + \"px\"; el.style.width = W + \"px\";\n  el.style.height = (bottom - top + (i < count - 1 ? 1 : 0)) + \"px\";\n  var copy = stripIds(src.cloneNode(true));\n  copy.classList.add(\"vnb-copy\");\n  copy.style.position = \"absolute\"; copy.style.top = -top + \"px\"; copy.style.left = \"0\"; copy.style.width = W + \"px\"; copy.style.height = H + \"px\";\n  var sh = document.createElement(\"div\");\n  sh.className = \"vnb-shade\"; sh.style.background = shade; sh.style.opacity = 0;\n  el.appendChild(copy); el.appendChild(sh); host.appendChild(el);\n  var t = count > 1 ? i / (count - 1) : 0;\n  var delay = dir === \"bottom-up\" ? 1 - t : dir === \"center\" ? Math.abs(t - 0.5) * 2 : t;\n  slats.push({ el: el, sh: sh, start: delay * spread });\n}\nfunction frame(p) {\n  var s = interp(p, [0, 1], [1.06, 1], outCubic);\n  B.style.transform = \"scale(\" + s + \")\";\n  for (var i = 0; i < slats.length; i++) {\n    var sl = slats[i];\n    var local = turn(interp(p, [sl.start, sl.start + 1 - spread], [0, 1]));\n    var angle = local * 90, fade = interp(angle, [76, 88], [1, 0]);\n    sl.el.style.display = fade <= 0 ? \"none\" : \"block\";\n    sl.el.style.transform = \"rotateX(\" + angle + \"deg)\";\n    sl.el.style.opacity = fade;\n    sl.sh.style.opacity = Math.sin(angle * Math.PI / 180) * 0.75;\n  }\n}\n\n            drive(\"venetian-blinds\", D, frame);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
